, its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"text":" the same way when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"props"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, flattened; left out when there are none"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"systemProps","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, "},{"code":"isDebug","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"sdkVersion","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601, in UTC with milliseconds"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"systemProps","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds ","type":"text"},{"code":"osName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"osVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"appVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"appBuildNumber","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"deviceModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s language and region (","type":"text"},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), each left out when the context has no value for it;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isDebug","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the encoder is made with; and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sdkVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Aptabase requires, always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A member longer than Aptabase takes (30 characters of the system’s name, 100 of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its version, 50 of the app’s version, 20 of its build and 100 of the device’s model, counted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in UTF-16) is left out and the event is sent without it, as Aptabase refuses the whole request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holding one. The encoder logs a notice the first time it leaves out each member.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: Aptabase has no member for a user or a device. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or one a store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is a session of its own: Aptabase takes no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event without a session. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and other context","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values aren’t sent. Aptabase counts users itself, from a hash of each request’s IP address and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"User-Agent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" header field with a salt it changes every day.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, and so is an element of an array. Aptabase stores a string, a number or a boolean as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property’s value, and only a placeholder for an object or array, so an object or array is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spread into a property per value it holds, named after its path, joined by ","type":"text"},{"code":".","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"cart.size","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"tags.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left out.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" doesn’t describe; one whose event name is only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whitespace or over 60 characters; one with a property whose name, once flattened, is empty, only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whitespace or over 40 characters, whose string value is over 180 characters, or whose number is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"too large for Aptabase; one whose values flatten to one name; one whose event isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":"; one that holds a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"JSON can’t; one whose timestamp is outside the years 1 to 9999, or more than 23 hours before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the batch is encoded; and one too large for a request (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":"s, which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" logs and reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, gives each a deadline 23 hours after its oldest record was tracked, and makes none for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for it. Aptabase"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t remove duplicates, so a record sent again, after a retry whose answer was lost or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store’s redelivery, is counted twice. The bytes are the same for the same records on every run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/aptabasebatchencoder"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"references":{"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding":{"title":"AptabaseEncoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to Aptabase, in its cloud or on your own server, through its events API."}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding/AptabaseBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase’s limits on one request: 25 events, and 1,000,000 bytes of body and of one event."}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","title":"batchLimit","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/aptabasebatchencoder\/batchlimit","role":"symbol"},"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding/AptabaseBatchEncoder/Failure":{"title":"AptabaseBatchEncoder.Failure","url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/aptabasebatchencoder\/failure","abstract":[{"text":"Why a record was left out of